{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Goal\n\nRemove the legacy `rebar reconcile --mode reconcile-check` CLI/direct-engine command and its persisted `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` artifact without breaking the canonical bridge surfaces that replaced its observables.\n\nThe replacement is intentionally distributed (ticket 3b66 \"Migrate bridge reconcile diagnostics\"):\n- `rebar bridge preview` is the live Jira-vs-local differ/proposed-change observable.\n- `rebar bridge fsck --output json` is the offline orphan/unbound/binding-drift audit observable.\n- `rebar bridge status --json` remains the status surface, but it must stop reading the stale legacy `reconcile-check.json` artifact once the writer is deleted.\n\nThe pause sentinel string `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"` is NOT the CLI command and must be preserved byte-for-byte.\n\n## Scope\n\nRemove the CLI/direct-engine reconcile-check command path and every caller owned by this ticket:\n\n- `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py`: repoint the retained `reconcile-check` runner profile to canonical `rebar bridge preview`, not `bridge fsck`.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`: remove the legacy top-level `rebar reconcile` route registration.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/reconcile.py`: remove legacy `--mode reconcile-check` parser exposure and the `--filter-local-ids` CLI surface.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/reconcile.txt`: remove generated/static help for the removed legacy CLI surface.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`: delete `_run_reconcile_check`, delete the dispatch branch for `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK`, and remove CLI-only `filter_local_ids` handoff from this route.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py`: remove legacy-route parsing for `--mode reconcile-check` and `--filter-local-ids`; keep canonical `preview`/`sync` normalization.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py`: remove `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK`, its `_ORDERED` entry, and its `MODE_CAPS` entry.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_preflight.py`: remove reconcile-check from no-write/preflight documentation and logic.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py`: remove `_read_reconcile_diagnostics()` and stop surfacing `reconcile_diagnostics` from `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_check.py`: delete the orphaned legacy report module; canonical preview/fsck/status do not import it.\n- Update stale in-code comments/docstrings in `binding_recovery.py`, `binding_walk.py`, `fetcher.py`, `get_rotation.py`, `load_phase.py`, `pass_support.py`, `reconcile_helpers.py`, and `ticket_planner.py` so remaining no-write wording refers to `dry-run`/`preview`, not reconcile-check.\n- Remove the retired `reconcile_diagnostics` field from `src/rebar/schemas/bridge_status.schema.json` and its typing in `src/rebar/types.py`.\n- Update bridge workflow/probe/docs/changelog references that instruct operators to invoke `reconcile-check`, replacing them with `bridge preview` for live discrepancy checks and `bridge fsck --output json` for orphan/unbound audits.\n- Update or remove tests that directly exercise the deleted CLI command/module; add regression coverage for the canonical replacements and pause-sentinel preservation.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n1. `bridge fsck` is NOT the sole replacement for `reconcile-check`. It is an offline audit over committed event/binding state and can intentionally exit `1` for audit findings. It does not provide the same live Jira-vs-local discrepancy report or legacy success semantics.\n2. `_bridge_runner.py` must map the retained `reconcile-check` profile to `rebar bridge preview`. The runner treats nonzero provider exits as operational failures and skips delivery, so mapping to `bridge fsck` would make ordinary fsck findings look like runner failures.\n3. `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` has no canonical writer after `_run_reconcile_check` is deleted. Do NOT invent a new writer. Remove the `last_pass.py` reader so `bridge status` cannot report stale diagnostics.\n4. Preserve `_ref_lock.py` pause documents exactly: `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"` remains the live pause sentinel and is semantically distinct from the removed CLI command. `_ref_lock.py` is intentionally NOT in the edit set.\n5. Do not remove dead internal `filter_local_ids` engine plumbing beyond this ticket's CLI surface. That cleanup belongs to follow-up `f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0`.\n6. Do not edit `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` or `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`; public Python/MCP `rebar.reconcile(mode=...)` compatibility belongs to sibling `c195-03cd-fc03-4ae0`, which MUST land before this ticket (recorded `depends_on`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py` proves `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK`, `_ORDERED[\"reconcile-check\"]`, and `MODE_CAPS[RECONCILE_CHECK]` are gone while dry-run/bootstrap/live ordering still works.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py` proves `python -m rebar_reconciler --mode reconcile-check` is rejected as an unknown mode and `_run_reconcile_check` is no longer dispatched.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py` proves `_bridge_runner.MODE_COMMANDS[\"reconcile-check\"]` invokes `rebar bridge preview`, preserves runner delivery semantics, and does not map to `bridge fsck`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py` proves orphaned bindings, orphaned Jira, unbound local, and unbound Jira remain available through canonical `bridge fsck --output json`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py` proves `bridge status` still reports last-pass/pause/live-lock status but no longer reads or surfaces stale `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py` proves pause documents still preserve `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"` byte-for-byte.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_reconcile_check_cli_removal_heldout.py` is the held-out oracle proving the removed CLI spelling is rejected, the canonical replacement guidance is present, and `git grep \"reconcile-check\" -- src/rebar tests docs .github Jenkinsfile scripts` only finds the preserved pause sentinel or explicitly documented historical/changelog references.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `env GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=4 GIT_CONFIG_KEY_3=safe.bareRepository GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_3=all PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test` passes.\n\n## Testing\n\nHeld-out oracle: add/maintain `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_reconcile_check_cli_removal_heldout.py` to prove the deleted command stays deleted, `_bridge_runner` points to `bridge preview`, and pause-sentinel files are excluded from removal.\n\nTargeted tests:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_reconcile_check_cli_removal_heldout.py`\n\nFull gates: `make test` (with the env-artifact sanitizer above), `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Do not edit `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` or `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`; c195 removes Python/MCP `rebar.reconcile(mode=...)`.\n- Do not remove engine `filter_local_ids` plumbing beyond the CLI surface; follow-up `f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0` owns that dead plumbing.\n- Do not change `_ref_lock.py` pause sentinel bytes or pause document schema.\n- Do not change canonical `bridge preview`, `bridge sync`, `bridge fsck`, or `bridge status` semantics except removing stale `reconcile_diagnostics` file consumption."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788485653940774063,"uuid":"852291e0-45f4-4312-a21a-9276a4744295"}